# BusyBox applets for the flasher's init and the Lemnos init scripts (Lemnos packaging/init, b0bf0101).
# Gaia's Buildroot base is allnoconfig, so an applet is on only when this file says so. Each line:
# ash        /bin/sh: the Lemnos scripts are POSIX sh run under ash, and rcS runs them
# init       PID 1 (BR2_INIT_BUSYBOX): /etc/inittab and rcS
# getty      the console getty on ttyGS0 (BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY)
# login      what getty starts for a login (root without a password, the console policy in the OS fragment)
# mount      rcS mounts proc, sys and devtmpfs
# start-stop-daemon  S50lemnosd and S51lemnos-orion start their supervisors with it (the script says so)
# mdev       device nodes at boot (mdev -s) and on hotplug; the Lemnos rules are an mdev.conf fragment
# sleep, kill, cat, date, rm, mkdir, touch, dirname, test ([)  used by the two init scripts
# sync, reboot, poweroff, halt  the shutdown path of init
CONFIG_ASH=y
CONFIG_INIT=y
CONFIG_GETTY=y
CONFIG_LOGIN=y
CONFIG_MOUNT=y
CONFIG_UMOUNT=y
CONFIG_START_STOP_DAEMON=y
CONFIG_MDEV=y
CONFIG_FEATURE_MDEV_CONF=y
CONFIG_SLEEP=y
CONFIG_KILL=y
CONFIG_CAT=y
CONFIG_DATE=y
CONFIG_RM=y
CONFIG_MKDIR=y
CONFIG_TOUCH=y
CONFIG_DIRNAME=y
CONFIG_TEST=y
CONFIG_SYNC=y
CONFIG_REBOOT=y
CONFIG_POWEROFF=y
CONFIG_HALT=y
